cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Testuary, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Testuary"
abstract: >-
  Testuary writes unit tests for Python, Java and C code with a language
  model. It runs the tests, measures which lines and branches they cover and
  how many mutants (small deliberate bugs) they catch, and asks the model for
  more tests wherever something is still missed, until your goals or limits
  are reached. It then keeps only the tests that add coverage or catch an
  extra mutant, and hands you the finished test suite with its measurements.
authors:
  - family-names: "Kammler"
    given-names: "Kevin"
license: MIT
version: "0.2.0"
keywords:
  - test generation
  - mutation testing
  - large language models
  - automated testing
repository-code: "https://github.com/k-kammler/testuary"
url: "https://github.com/k-kammler/testuary"
